<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Yang et al. (2022) & Donnay & Pawson (1969) biogenic single-crystal calcite TPMS echinoderm stereom (Diamond D, Gyroid G, Primitive P) & Gibson-Ashby cellular mechanics — Model fidelity to source: 54/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Evaluates a 2D slice of Schoen Gyroid F_G(x,y,z) and a 1D Gibson–Ashby scaling curve (L29-55), but lacks 3D TPMS voxel and implicit-surface differential geometry (mean curvature H = 0 and Gaussian curvature K = -kappa_1^2 <= 0) across Diamond D, Gyroid G, Primitive P, and stochastic spinodal stereom, omits super-threshold pinch-off ablation (c = 1.35), and omits crystallographic [111] vs [100] projections." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py L29–L55: 2D Gyroid slice and 1D Gibson-Ashby curve without 3D TPMS curvature, topology, or Diamond/Primitive families <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/HEAD/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py#L29-L55>" ;
    pk:hasScore 5.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

